# / AArch64 Xiaomi Pad 5
# Maintainer: Kumar-Jy
# Kernel 6.16.0-8 = rodriguezst recipe + wakeup fix (0050) + SMB5
# backport (0051-0054: qcom_smbx charger) replacing ln8000. SMB5 adds the
# PM8150B PMIC charger block (USBIN + ADC), so 5V USB / QC3 A-to-C charging
# now works. 0050 defers the MI blank-notify from pre_enable to enable time
# on a workqueue (panel-live wakeup, no atomic-commit deadlock). The SM8150
# camss series (old 0051-0055) is dropped: it enabled camss/cci at boot,
# which the ABL bootloader rejects (gray-screen reset) and
# caused a no-console CAMSS probe hang on this port.
# pkgrel 17: camera bring-up test (0059-0064). Re-adds the SM8150 camss
# driver (0059) + sm8150 camss/cci DT nodes (0061) + ov13b10 compatible
# (0062), with camcc now built (CONFIG_SM_CAMCC_8150=m, was the missing clock
# controller that made the old camss probe hang). Board sensor nodes (0063)
# and all camss/cci/camcc remain 'disabled' so default boot is UNCHANGED
# (no ABL gray-screen reset); enable them via the derived (0064)
# sm8150-xiaomi-nabu-camera.dtb for on-device probe. Verified: camss compiles
# against 6.16; 0059-0064 series applies cleanly to pristine 6.16 via the
# makepkg 'patch -Np1' invocation (all 65 patches, no fuzz/rejects).
# pkgrel 8 (0051): add CHGR_CFG2 to smb5_init_seq so charge termination /
# auto-recharge / inhibit are set to sane defaults; without it the PM8150b
# can sit in INHIBIT/TERMINATE and report FULL at a low state of charge,
# which also propagated to the fuel gauge via its power-supply notifier.
# pkgrel 9: rebuild of identical pkgrel-8 source. The 6.16.0-8 CI build lost
# the qcom_smbx driver at link time (CI GCC 16.1.1 dropped smb_probe / the
# platform-driver registration), leaving only its data tables; the running
# kernel had no charger. Source set unchanged; retry to confirm the -8 drop
# was a one-off CI-GCC flake (the complete 0051 builds the driver fine
# locally: smb_probe + qcom_spmi_smb present, no -Wunused-function).
# pkgrel 10 (0051): the -9 rebuild reproduced the same loss - CI GCC 16.1.1
# deterministically prunes the whole module_platform_driver registration
# (initcall + qcom_spmi_smb struct + smb_probe) out of qcom_smbx.c. Fix:
# replace module_platform_driver with an explicit __used device_initcall
# (qcom_spmi_smb_init/exit) and mark smb_probe __used, so the registration
# is anchored in the initcall section and cannot be dead-code eliminated.
# pkgrel 11 (0014b): the same CI GCC 16.1.1 dead-code elimination that pruned
# qcom_smbx also strips qcom_fg (the built-in CONFIG_BATTERY_QCOM_FG fuel
# gauge / battery driver): its static qcom_fg_probe + module_platform_driver
# registration vanish at link time, so 6.16.0-8/9/10 had no qcom-battery psy
# and the charger could not read battery status. Fix is applied as a separate
# patch (0014b) AFTER 0014 rather than editing 0013: modifying 0013 shifts the
# source lines that 0014's hunks target, and GNU patch (used by makepkg) then
# truncates the qcom_fg.c tail (qcom_fg_exit body), breaking the build. So 0013
# stays stock and 0014b marks qcom_fg_probe __used and replaces
# module_platform_driver with an explicit __used device_initcall
# (qcom_fg_init/exit) on the final source.
# pkgrel 12 (0051): on-device test of pkgrel-11 (6.16.0-11) showed the fuel
# gauge now binds (deferred probe msg) but qcom-battery still never appears:
# the battery's power-supplies phandle points at the charger, and the charger
# (qcom_smbx) is STILL absent. Root cause found in 0051 itself: its diff
# header declares "1131 insertions" / "@@ -0,0 +1,1131 @@", but the body
# actually carries 1153 '+ ' lines (the __used device_initcall registration
# added in pkgrel-10 was folded in without recomputing the count). GNU patch
# (makepkg) trusts the declared count and silently truncates the 22 trailing
# lines - the whole qcom_spmi_smb driver struct + device_initcall + exit are
# dropped, so the charger could never bind in 6.16.0-8/-9/-10/-11. Fix: set
# the header to "1153 insertions" / "@@ -0,0 +1,1153 @@" so the full driver
# survives, and additionally mark smb_match_id_table[] + qcom_spmi_smb __used
# so CI GCC 16.1.1 + -fdata-sections/--gc-sections cannot GC the of-match and
# driver data at link time.
# pkgrel 13 (0055): PD (USB-C to USB-C) still never charges: the SMB5 block
# only performs APSD-based detection (SDP/CDP/DCP) and has no USB-PD
# awareness, so a PD source is reported as "Unknown SDP" with a 500mA limit,
# battery status stays FULL and the battery discharges. Follow the proven
# LN8000 approach - reference the type-c port psy via the "usb-tcpm" phandle,
# register a power-supply notifier, and when a PD/PPS source comes online set
# the input current limit from battery info, clear USBIN suspend and let
# hardware charge.
# pkgrel 14 (0056+0057): two follow-ups. 0056: the type-c notifier set the
# USBIN suspend bit on online=0 and only cleared it for PD sources, so legacy
# USB-A to USB-C chargers (APSD SDP/CDP/DCP) stayed suspended -> battery stuck
# at FULL while discharging; now the suspend bit is cleared for any attached
# source and APSD/type-c picks the input current limit. 0057: advertise only a
# fixed 5V/3A sink PDO (drop PDO_VAR 5000-9000) because the SMB5 block only
# charges from 5V; a 9V PD contract negotiated fine but never charged.

# pkgrel 21 (0070): ov13b10/ov8856 probe failed with -EINVAL ("no link
# frequencies defined") because the sensor endpoint nodes in 0063 don't carry
# a link-frequencies property - the upstream drivers require it on the
# sensor endpoint, while camss has it on its own remote endpoint. Rather than
# editing 0063 (which shifts the DTS tail and broke CI with a DTC syntax error
# at sm8150-xiaomi-nabu.dts:1401), 0070 makes both drivers tolerate the
# missing property: link-frequency validation is skipped with a dev_dbg when
# the DT endpoint omits it. The drivers still operate with their own
# compiled-in mode/link-freq tables.
# pkgrel 22 (0063 fix): on-device camera-probe boot of pkgrel 21 failed:
# camss probe error "pin GPIO_17 already requested by ac4a000.cci; cannot
# claim for ac65000.camss" because 0063 put the mclk/reset/cci pinctrl groups
# on &camss, double-claiming GPIO17/18/19/20 that the cci nodes own (the
# docs-camera-bringup fix was to drop camss pinctrl-0, keeping only
# pinctrl-names). Also ov8856 probe failed with "no link frequency 720000000
# supported" - the sensor endpoint only listed 360 MHz while the driver's
# 2-lane menu wants 720+360. 0063 now drops the camss pinctrl-0 block and
# lists 720000000 360000000 on the ov8856 endpoint (matches CFM880 <720 360>).
# pkgrel 23 (boot/install parity): bring the package boot plumbing up to the
# fully-working 6.14 baseline - inline UKI mkinitcpio preset, stable /boot
# symlinks (vmlinuz-/dtb-linux-nabu), iris/venus blacklist, and the
# linux-nabu.install hook that regenerates the UKI and pins uki.conf
# DeviceTree to the current DTB. Now installable as a direct UKI boot like 6.14.
#
# pkgrel 24 (SLPI accelerometer): enable the ST accel through the SLPI
# remoteproc + FastRPC protection-domain stack like the 6.14 baseline.
# 0071 backports the CFM880 FastRPC PDR attach + SDSP IOVA alias workaround
# (driver, binding, qcom_pd_mapper domains) to 6.16; 0072 turns on
# &remoteproc_slpi and adds the msm/slpi/root_pd compute contexts in the
# nabu DTS. iris/venus remain blacklisted (SLPI is the boot-default stack).

